        "body": "[BUG-FIXER-TRIAGE] Classification: T4 (project-candidate)\n\n**Why T4:**\n- Estimated scope: Cross-cutting across ~14+ files spanning `scripts/` (all dispatchers, `install.sh`, `configure.sh`, `safe_ingest.py`, `liveness.py`), `skills/` (triage, engineering, architect-review), `docs/`, `rules/`, and `config.json`. Estimated >500 lines changed.\n- Requires architectural decisions: Yes. Renaming core GitHub labels (`auto-fixable`, `human-required`, `needs-approach-review`, `needs-iteration`, `status:in-progress`, etc.) has cross-repo dependency implications. Requires defining a consistent namespace schema (e.g. `bug-fixer:auto-fixable` vs `bug-fixer:in-progress`), backward compatibility / migration strategy for existing repositories and open issues, and updating config schemas.\n- Suggested decomposition:\n  1. Define unified label taxonomy and migration/compatibility design in specification\n  2. Update configuration schema, `configure.sh`, and `install.sh`\n  3. Update dispatchers (`engineering_dispatcher.py`, `triage_dispatcher.py`, `architect_dispatcher.py`, `trajectory_dispatcher.py`) and `safe_ingest.py`\n  4. Update skill markdown files, prompts, and documentation\n  5. Add migration utility for existing target repositories\n\n**Recommendation:** Use /principal-architect to decompose into work orders.",
