  {
    "number": 15,
    "title": "[BugFixer-Health] 24h Trajectory Review: Dispatcher Churn, MCP Lock Contention, and Uncommitted Dispatcher Fix",
    "labels": [],
    "body": "## Bug Fixer Loop Health Report (24h Trajectory Review)\n\n**Review Period:** 2026-09-28 07:42 UTC \u2013 2026-09-29 07:42 UTC  \n**Scope:** 15 sessions (14 tick, 1 triage), 7 PRs opened, 6 merged, 100% test pass rate.\n\n---\n\n### Critical Operational Patterns Detected\n\n#### 1. Dispatcher Re-Spawn Churn Loop (7 Redundant Sessions)\n- **Symptom:** After issues #254, #255, and #256 were fixed and PRs (#268, #267, #266) opened at ~19:40\u201319:46 UTC, `tick_dispatcher.py` repeatedly claimed them again and spawned 7 redundant agent conversations at 19:41, 19:51, and 20:01 UTC.\n- **Root Cause:** In `scripts/tick_dispatcher.py` (Step 3), eligible issue filtering only excluded `status:in-progress`, but omitted `status:awaiting-review`.\n- **Hot-Patch Applied:** Locally patched at 21:04 UTC to exclude `(\"status:in-progress\", \"status:awaiting-review\")` and refine PR search logic.\n- **Action Required:** The hot-patch in `.agents/plugins/bug-fixer-loop-plugin/scripts/tick_dispatcher.py` is currently **uncommitted** in the plugin git tree and should be committed.\n\n#### 2. PlatformIO MCP Exclusive Lock Contention (2hr Worker Starvation)\n- **Symptom:** Sessions `ddd7f636` (Issue #234) and `3b62a4f0` (Issue #241) stalled for over 2 hours with `Hardware is currently tied` errors.\n- **Root Cause:** Session `c2b13ae1` (Issue #183) ran native unit tests via `platformio-mcp_platformio`, which acquired the exclusive environment lock, but exited without releasing it until manual maintainer intervention at 15:23 UTC.\n- **Action Required:** Mandate explicit `release_lock` invocation in `bug-fixer-tick/SKILL.md` teardown, and add automated lock recovery/timeout in the dispatcher.\n\n#### 3. AgentAPI Offline / Label Churn During Unattended Ticks\n- **Symptom:** Between 12:01 and 18:40 UTC, the sidecar cron executed every 10 minutes while `agentapi` was unreachable. This triggered rapid add/remove of `status:in-progress` and tripped the circuit breaker across 5 separate 1-hour cooldown cycles.\n- **Action Required:** In `tick_dispatcher.py`, ping/verify `agentapi` daemon responsiveness before updating GitHub issue labels.\n\n---\n_Note: Originally filed as esp32-app-foundation#269 but transferred here since it requires changes to the bug-fixer loop plugin itself._",
